# MORNIN.
## COMPLETE PRODUCT REQUIREMENTS DOCUMENT (PRD) & FULL-STACK DEVELOPMENT PROMPT

You are an expert product designer, senior UI/UX designer, software architect, and full-stack React developer.

Your task is to design, develop, and implement a complete, functional, premium-quality web application named **MORNIN.**

This is a complete product development task, not just a landing page, UI mockup, or static prototype.

You must build a real interactive application with working features, functional navigation, persistent data, responsive layouts, and a consistent visual identity.

Read and follow all requirements carefully.

==================================================
# PART 1 — PRODUCT OVERVIEW
==================================================

## 1.1 Product Identity

Product Name: MORNIN.

Tagline: Wake Up. Get Ready. Get Going.

Alternative Brand Statement: A calmer way to start your day.

Product Category: Morning Productivity & Lifestyle Companion.

Platform: Responsive Web Application, optimized for mobile devices.

Target Users:
- University students.
- High school students.
- Young professionals.
- Office workers.
- Individuals with busy daily schedules.
- People who want to improve their morning routines.

## 1.2 Product Vision

MORNIN is a personal morning companion designed to make everyday mornings easier, more organized, and more enjoyable.

It combines five essential morning activities into one application:

1. Waking up with an interactive alarm.
2. Reviewing and managing today's activities.
3. Discovering breakfast recommendations.
4. Checking essential belongings before leaving home.
5. Tracking morning readiness and daily progress.

MORNIN should guide users through their morning without overwhelming them with too much information.

The product should feel like a personal lifestyle assistant rather than a complicated productivity management system.

## 1.3 Core Value Proposition

"Everything you need to start your day, in one calm and simple place."

The application must prioritize simplicity, convenience, and clarity.

Users should be able to understand what they need to do immediately after opening the application.

