# PART 2 — DESIGN PHILOSOPHY & BRAND IDENTITY
==================================================

THIS SECTION IS EXTREMELY IMPORTANT.

The overall visual direction must be inspired by Apple's design philosophy and native iOS applications.

Reference the visual simplicity and interaction patterns of:
- Apple Clock.
- Apple Reminders.
- Apple Weather.
- Apple Health.
- Apple Calendar.

Do not directly copy Apple's branding or interface. Develop an original MORNIN identity while following similar design principles.

## 2.1 Design Philosophy

The main principle is:

LESS UI. MORE CLARITY.

The application must be:
- Minimalist.
- Elegant.
- Premium.
- Calm.
- Intuitive.
- Modern.
- Friendly.
- Effortless to use.

Avoid conventional productivity dashboards that contain too many cards, buttons, widgets, graphs, and decorative elements.

Do not fill every empty space with UI components.

Whitespace is an important part of the design.

## 2.2 Color Palette

Use a restrained and sophisticated palette.

Primary background:
#FAFAF8

Secondary background:
#F3F2ED

White surface:
#FFFFFF

Primary text:
#242424

Secondary text:
#92958E

Primary accent:
#E9D58D

Soft accent:
