Use off-white and white as the dominant colors.

Use soft yellow/gold only for important highlights, active elements, and selected states.

Avoid excessive colors, strong gradients, and saturated backgrounds.

## 2.3 Typography

Use Manrope as the primary typeface, or a similar modern sans-serif font.

Typography should resemble the clean and elegant feeling of SF Pro Display.

Typography hierarchy:

- Large display typography for the clock.
- Medium-weight typography for page titles.
- Regular typography for descriptions.
- Small muted typography for metadata.
- Semibold typography for important information.

Avoid excessive bold text.

## 2.4 Components and Layout

Use:
- Rounded corners between 14px and 20px.
- Thin separators.
- Minimal borders.
- Very subtle shadows.
- Simple iOS-inspired toggles.
- Minimal circular checkboxes.
- Clean line icons.
- Consistent spacing.
- Smooth transitions.

Use Lucide React icons.

Do not use large decorative icons or unnecessary illustrations.

## 2.5 Button Philosophy

Buttons must be minimal.

Each screen should have one primary action at most.

Use simple text buttons, understated icon buttons, and native-looking controls.

Do not place multiple action buttons inside every card.

Use small floating or top-right add actions only when necessary.

Avoid oversized colorful buttons.

## 2.6 Responsive Design

Prioritize the mobile experience.

The application should feel natural on an iPhone-sized screen.

Use:
- Mobile safe-area spacing.
- Comfortable touch targets.
- Responsive typography.
- Fixed bottom navigation.
- Clean vertical scrolling.
- Minimal horizontal scrolling.

On desktop, use a compact navigation sidebar or top navigation while maintaining the same visual identity.

