# PART 5 — ALARM & WAKE-UP CHALLENGE
==================================================

The Alarm feature is one of the core functions of MORNIN.

Its purpose is to encourage users to wake up actively instead of dismissing an alarm automatically.

## 5.1 Alarm Management

Allow users to:

- Create alarms.
- Edit alarms.
- Delete alarms.
- Enable or disable alarms.
- Set alarm times.
- Choose recurring days.
- Add alarm labels.
- Choose a wake-up challenge.
- Configure snooze duration.

Alarm interface:

Use an iOS Clock-inspired layout.

Each alarm should display:
- Large time.
- Label.
- Repeat schedule.
- Minimal toggle switch.

Use a simple add alarm button.

Avoid unnecessary alarm cards.

## 5.2 Alarm Configuration

When creating an alarm, provide:

- Time picker.
- AM/PM or 24-hour format.
- Repeat days.
- Alarm label.
- Challenge type.
- Challenge difficulty.
- Snooze duration.

Use a clean modal or dedicated configuration sheet.

## 5.3 Wake-Up Challenges

Provide three mini games.

A. MATH CHALLENGE

The user must solve a basic arithmetic problem.

Examples:
- 17 + 26.
- 45 - 18.
- 8 × 7.

Difficulty:
- Easy.
- Medium.
- Hard.

B. MEMORY MATCH

Display a small grid of hidden cards.

The user must find matching pairs.

Requirements:
- Flip card interaction.
- Match detection.
- Simple completion state.
- Minimal game interface.

C. PATTERN RECOGNITION

Display a sequence of numbers or symbols.

The user must identify the missing element.

Example:

2, 4, 6, ?, 10.

The user enters the correct answer to complete the challenge.

## 5.4 Alarm Experience

When the alarm reaches its configured time:

1. Show an alarm screen.
2. Display the alarm label and time.
3. Start an alarm sound where supported.
4. Present the selected challenge.
5. Require successful completion before dismissal.
6. Stop the sound after successful completion.
7. Update the morning progress.

Show a message:

"Good morning! You're officially up."

## 5.5 Snooze

Allow users to snooze the alarm.

Provide configurable snooze durations:
- 5 minutes.
- 10 minutes.
- 15 minutes.

Use a simple snooze action.

## 5.6 Technical Limitations

IMPORTANT:

This is initially a browser-based web application.

Implement alarm scheduling using browser-compatible mechanisms.

Use browser notifications where supported and permission is granted.

Do not claim that a web alarm will reliably sound while the browser is completely closed or the device is sleeping.

Provide an in-app alarm simulation/testing mode.

Keep alarm configuration and challenge logic modular so native Android/iOS alarm functionality can be integrated in the future.

